  "summary": "Bundled cryptominer routed to hardcoded author wallet",
  "details": "The package advertises itself in README as 'a simple Python installer program' but ships a ~32MB bundled Rust/CUDA GPU cryptominer (animated_octo_spoon/forge, identifying as ForgeMiner/1.4.1 with stratum/mining.authorize protocol strings and cubin kernels for kawpow/xelis/cryptix/keryx). The CLI entrypoint (cli.main) locates start.sh alongside the package, chmods it 0755, and subprocess.runs it; start.sh in turn chmods and executes the bundled forge ELF with a hardcoded author wallet address (prl1p2jan4dvkdfkt5r3pra7z96axrxjyjcgat9w7ldetlcy9wffm569sc9ux2t) and a hardcoded stratum pool at 45.151.62.119:3361. Running the advertised CLI silently converts the installer's GPU and electricity into mining revenue routed to the author-controlled wallet. The declared purpose (Python installer) is a cover story for the actual behavior (hidden cryptominer with hardcoded payout).",
